WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.350
Unit 2 starts with the principals.

2
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:07.388
Create login, from external provider, maps
a login to one of three Entra principals.

3
00:00:07.388 --> 00:00:09.863
A user, named by its U P N.

4
00:00:09.863 --> 00:00:12.825
A security group, named
by its display name.

5
00:00:12.825 --> 00:00:15.625
Or an application, also by display name.

6
00:00:15.625 --> 00:00:17.537
In sys dot server principals,

7
00:00:17.537 --> 00:00:21.282
users and applications show as
type E, and groups as type X.

8
00:00:21.282 --> 00:00:25.425
Group logins are the target,
because they remove per-user churn.

9
00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:29.102
And an application's sequel login
with a stored password becomes

10
00:00:29.102 --> 00:00:32.438
an Entra application login,
preferably a managed identity.

11
00:00:32.438 --> 00:00:35.938
Create user, from login, then
makes the database user.

12
00:00:35.938 --> 00:00:39.838
One more thing to keep in mind:
the engine has no M F A logic.

13
00:00:39.838 --> 00:00:43.200
Conditional Access decides
before the token is issued.
